  "note": "Extracted by hand from the two schematics on one sheet, folded into one grammar: the FB6C 3A form prints the hard seats alone and the FB6CHT high temp form, not 3A, the full seat ladder. The high temp ladder prints the character 4 twice, first at the 0.6 PEEK seat and again at the 26.3 PEEK seat, so the first printing is carried and choosing 4 raises a caution, the 4700 precedent; the 26.3 PEEK row is left uncoded. The EE and VJ o-rings, the TY o-ring and the EPDM diaphragm keep their printed size brackets. The body Cv letters are matched to the trim rows as an inferred coupling.",
